;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 (written by Claude, from design section 16,
;; rtl/vax/Files.Mod and the guest run; for the user's review). Why this
;; is right:
;; - The same message as LLVM's, after an empty record as LLVM's starts
;;   with a line end, but naming the file as the program gave it:
;;   rtl/vax's Files gives a name to RMS as it is (its header), where
;;   rtl/llvm's makes it absolute. RMS cannot create no-such-
;;   directory/data, so Files' first Write, which makes the file on
;;   disk, stops the program (standard output and the status, 99, are
;;   the host's).

-- file not created: no-such-directory/data
